models looking good its Porsche classic  Department offers original replacement  parts for vehicles from years past  to mark the 40th anniversary of Porsches  transaxle technology over 100 privately  owned cars are taking part in a parade  but before the convoy sets off drivers  gather for a photo leading the way is  this 924 GTP sports car with legendary  racecar driver Derek bell at the wheel  they'll have a feeling because it's what  I raced at Lava in 1980 so to sort of  get back in the car again after what  whatever that is 35 years is pretty  special  but it felt just the same as I remember  it but of course in those days we just  went for it there was nobody in front so  you just went flat out and they were  it's so easy to drive then they're off  though here they're not allowed to  overtake one another this is a parade  just for show not a race all manner of  Porsches zoom around the circuit but  they do have one thing in common all  feature a front engine and rear-wheel  drive  Jaguar has set up what looks like a  giant car lot at the Grand Prix here  current models like the f-type sports  car the XF sedan and Jags new  all-electric formula e race car stand  alongside vintage treasures like this  1966 XJ 13 now lovingly restored this  prototype was totalled back in 1971 when  a wheel came off during the filming of a  promotional video Norman doiis was  Jaguars chief card tester for 33 years  he says the car could have had a great  career in motorsport it would have been  a good winner for LeMond one thing you  gon do is test the drivers you can't do  that  but if it have been Jim correct me would  have won I think whether it's 5 liter 12  cylinder engine and an output of 369  kilowatts the XJ 13 certainly had the  prerequisites but Jaguar abandoned the  project in 1967 instead the C D and E  type brought the British company acclaim  on the racing circuit and those models  got to take to the track once again  for the Grand Prix at the nürburgring  other manufacturers such as Ferrari  Maserati and Alfa Romeo are also here  showing off both old and new models  Pinal says events like this provide the  perfect platform to present vintage  vehicles and an opportunity to introduce  supercars  that's what McLaren is doing - taking  the opportunity to show off its latest  supercars like this six 50s  and next time on drive it a classic  updated the new e-class station wagon  from Mercedes and small and sporty with  a soft top the Mazda mx-5
 

